<div class="page-head">
  <div>
    <h1>Enforcement macros</h1>
    <p class="page-note">
      Canned action-and-reason combinations. Applying one records the wording it
      carries, so the same violation is described the same way by every
      operator instead of being retyped each time.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<%# The blind spot of a one-step action is that it hides its own guards, so the
    panel leads with what a macro is not. An operator who believes a macro
    carries authority would reach for it when the hand-written form is what is
    actually needed. %>
<div class="panel">
  <h3 class="panel-title">What a macro does and does not do</h3>
  <p class="muted">
    A macro supplies the action, the wording and the parameters. It grants no
    authority of its own: applying it still checks the acting operator's own
    permission for that action, still refuses their own account and still
    refuses an account at or above their rank. A permanent ban is deliberately
    not available as a macro, because it needs a second operator's approval and
    a one-step action would route around that.
  </p>
  <p class="muted">
    Disabling a macro keeps its row and its use count. The audit trail can then
    still name the macro an operator applied months ago, which deleting it would
    erase.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="panel">
  <h3 class="panel-title">New macro</h3>
  <% if can?('users.templates') %>
    <%= form_with url: admin_enforcement_templates_path, method: :post, class: "stack" do %>
      <label>Name
        <input type="text" name="name" maxlength="<%= EnforcementTemplate::MAX_NAME %>"
               placeholder="How operators will recognise it" required>
      </label>
      <label>Action
        <select name="action_key">
          <% EnforcementTemplate::ACTIONS.each do |key, spec| %>
            <option value="<%= key %>"><%= spec[:label] %></option>
          <% end %>
        </select>
      </label>
      <label>Duration
        <select name="duration">
          <% EnforcementTemplate.duration_choices('warn').each do |value, label| %>
            <option value="<%= value %>"><%= label %></option>
          <% end %>
        </select>
        <span class="muted">Applies to warnings and timed bans.</span>
      </label>
      <label>Warning category
        <select name="category">
          <% UserWarning::CATEGORIES.each do |value, label| %>
            <option value="<%= value %>"><%= label %></option>
          <% end %>
        </select>
        <span class="muted">Only meaningful for a warning.</span>
      </label>
      <label>Reason (the wording that is recorded)
        <textarea name="reason" rows="3" maxlength="<%= EnforcementTemplate::MAX_REASON %>"
                  placeholder="e.g. Posting targeted harassment under the reply of another account."
                  required></textarea>
      </label>
      <button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit">Create macro</button>
    <% end %>
  <% else %>
    <p class="muted">You can see the macros but not change them.</p>
  <% end %>
</div>

<div class="panel">
  <h3 class="panel-title">
    The macros
    <span class="muted"><%= @active_count %> active</span>
  </h3>

  <% if @templates.present? %>
    <table class="data-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th class="id">ID</th><th>Name</th><th>Action</th><th>Recorded reason</th>
            <th class="num">Used</th><th>State</th><th></th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <% @templates.each do |template| %>
          <tr class="<%= 'row-muted' unless template.active %>">
            <td class="id"><%= template.id %></td>
            <td><strong><%= template.name %></strong></td>
            <td>
              <span class="tag tag-info"><%= template.action_label %></span>
              <% if template.duration.present? && EnforcementTemplate.duration_choices(template.action_key).any? %>
                <span class="muted"><%= template.duration_label %></span>
              <% end %>
              <% if template.category.present? %>
                <span class="muted"><%= template.category_label %></span>
              <% end %>
            </td>
            <td class="muted"><%= template.reason.truncate(140) %></td>
            <td class="num"><%= number_with_delimiter(template.uses_count) %></td>
            <td>
              <% if template.active %>
                <span class="tag tag-quiet">active</span>
              <% else %>
                <span class="tag tag-quiet">off</span>
              <% end %>
            </td>
            <td>
              <% if can?('users.templates') %>
                <%= button_to(template.active ? "Turn off" : "Turn on",
                              admin_enforcement_template_toggle_path(template),
                              class: "btn btn-mini", form_class: "inline") %>
              <% end %>
            </td>
          </tr>
        <% end %>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  <% else %>
    <p class="muted">No macros yet.</p>
  <% end %>
</div>
